+## Mandatory Versus Recommended
+
+Mandatory:
+
+- Preserve current behavior unless the requested change explicitly changes it.
+- Read exact source before security, compliance, payment, final validation, or exact code edits.
+- Keep `apt-principles` canonical for doctrine and this repo canonical for distribution and harness behavior.
+- Keep `docs/project-context.md` and `.agent-repo/local-overrides.md` project-owned.
+- Use `--dry-run` before writes to real target repos.
+- Do not overwrite existing target files unless `--force` is intentional.
+
+Recommended:
+
+- Use compressed context packs for discovery, planning, summarization, and cross-repo alignment.
+- Use Headroom or similar tools only as optional context-compression support.
+- Create a short improvement backlog after repo alignment work.
+- Prefer reusable templates and examples over long theory.
+
